    turnFlow: 'A pyramid of cards is built face-down (6-5-4-3-2-1). Each player receives cards face-down, looks once to memorise them, then may not look again. Cards are revealed from the pyramid one by one (bottom row left to right, then next row). When a card is revealed, any player may claim to hold the same face value and assign a penalty (drinks) to another player; that player may accept or call bluff. If bluff is called and the claimer had the card, the assigned player drinks double; if the claimer was bluffing, the claimer drinks double. Number of drinks often equals the pyramid row (e.g. row 3 = 3 drinks). Game ends when the pyramid is fully revealed.',
